  "ticket": "COORD-863",
  "description": "Registered same-name compatibility shims left at legacy coord/ paths by the COORD-589 engine migration. Paths are coord-relative. Each shim names its canonical engine target (always engine/<path>) and a kind: permanent shims are the stable adopter entrypoints listed in stable_entrypoints and stay at coord/scripts indefinitely; every other shim is removable once no live reference spells its legacy path. A removable internal-module shim is exactly `module.exports = require(resolveEngineModule(coordDir, \"engine-only:<path>\"))`; a CLI shim re-dispatches the engine module's main. An ES module shim (.mjs) re-exports the named and default bindings of its engine target by fixed relative specifier and, as a CLI shim, calls the engine main when it is the entrypoint. Test suites (*.test.js) are never entrypoints. coord/paths.js validates this file; the engine-coverage census keeps registered shims out of the production census.",
